      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "id": "Text-81918d83-b842-4c54-a1d4-4f6fa478531e",
        "text": "<p>\"No Plastic\" was one of the mottos of the festival. Keeping that in mind, the bag was made plastic free. Materials used to make this bag are- Muslin cloth, Kalamkari wooden block and Indigo dye.</p>",
        "style": "body",
        "align": "start",
        "measure": "normal",
        "layout": {
          "width": "text",
          "space": "s",
          "show": "all",
          "motion": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Heading",
      "props": {
        "id": "Heading-f85b7711-f43f-4602-9751-537f73b04b70",
        "text": "Storytelling",
        "size": "title",
        "level": "h2",
        "align": "start",
        "layout": {
          "width": "text",
          "space": "m",
          "show": "all",
          "motion": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "id": "Text-ed1a9a15-ffc7-49a9-b208-17e970f0d073",
        "text": "<p>The bag is made in a form of a 3 page comic. The fourth face of the bag contains the festival logo. The story depicted on the bag is a famous folklore of Andhra. The intent of picking up a local story was to establish the connection between the festival and the local culture. Bag being a take away from the festival, It was my intention to make the guests take back memories and experience from this place, by being part of Chitrakatha.</p>",
        "style": "body",
        "align": "start",
        "measure": "normal",
        "layout": {
          "width": "text",
          "space": "s",
          "show": "all",
          "motion": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "StudyImages",
      "props": {
        "id": "StudyImages-6a9081e2-8c87-445a-9bb9-0529a4d84072",
        "photos": [
